# Normalize to LF in the index and, crucially, in the WORKING TREE too.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true checks the tree out
# with CRLF. That silently breaks the `npm run check-embedded` merge gate: the
# committed dashboard bundle under crates/cli/assets/dashboard/dist/ becomes
# CRLF, while a fresh vite build emits mixed endings (CRLF passed through from
# the tracked source template, LF for vite's own injected tags), and the check
# is a byte comparison. A Windows contributor could not make that gate pass.
#
# `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is what pins the working tree, so it holds
# regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and anything with a shebang must stay LF to remain executable
# under bash/WSL and inside the Docker build context.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one place CRLF is the native convention. Windows PowerShell
# 5.1 in particular can mis-parse an LF-only script containing a here-string.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never transform, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
